---
description: On each merge/ship, bump displayed app version by +0.01 (until user switches to +1)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Version bump on merge / ship

## Default scheme (until user says otherwise)

Every time code is **merged to master** or **shipped** (commit + push + deploy of the live line), increment the **display version** by **+0.01** (patch-style).

Examples: `v21` → `v21.01` → `v21.02` → …

Later, if the user asks to switch to whole-step bumps, use **+1** instead (e.g. `v19` → `v21`, or `v20.97` → `v21`).

## What “version in code” means

Update these when bumping (keep them consistent):

| Surface | Examples |
|---------|----------|
| UI / header | `dashboardHeader` title (`The YNow App v21…`), About 文案, 意見區 / report strings that show app version |
| Docs in app tree | README / comments that state the current display version |
| Deploy notes | `scripts/DEPLOY_BASELINE.txt` note (and similar) may mention the display version |
| Deploy scripts | Keep targeting the live folder; rename scripts only on a full +1 cut if needed |

Do **not** invent a second version number; one display version for the live line.

## Folder vs display version

- **Live directory** is `app_24.0/` while display shows `v24`, `v24.01`, …
- **Directory rename** (e.g. `app_24.0/` → `app_24.0/`) only when the user requests the next full **+1** version cut. Set `YNOW_VERSION_BUMP_MAJOR=1` on that deploy so the display version becomes `vN.00`.
- If header/UI and folder naming disagree: **UI/header/version strings bump +0.01 each merge**; **folder stays** until that +1 cut.

## When to bump

- Yes: every **completed deploy** of the live line. `Rscript scripts/deploy_app_21.R` does this itself: it advances the display version by **+0.01**, commits that bump, then uploads. The bundle that finishes deploying is the incremented version.
- If the working tree is already exactly **+0.01** ahead of `scripts/DEPLOY_BASELINE.txt` `display_version`, the script ships that bump and does **not** add another 0.01 (so a retry is not a double bump).
- Skip only with `--no-bump` or `YNOW_SKIP_VERSION_BUMP=1`.
- No: docs-only / rules-only, exploratory WIP, or commits the user says not to ship. Do not bump by hand before calling the deploy script.
- This rule records policy only; do not bump “just because” the rule file was edited.

## Automatic step

Agents do not hand-edit `v23.xx` strings before deploy. The deploy script owns the +0.01 step (`scripts/bump_display_version.R`). Surfaces it rewrites: header / About / Lite copy in `ynow_ui.R`, `report_template.Rmd` `app_version`, the README title line, `www/ynow_build.json`, and a hardcoded header expectation in `tests/test_lite_mode_ui.R` when present. README history sections stay on their original version numbers. The app directory stays `app_24.0/` until the user asks for the next full +1 cut.
